<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenian Revoz says 96 net up 25.9 pct.</title>
<headline>Slovenian Revoz says 96 net up 25.9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-04-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenian car producer Revoz, a subsidiary of France's Renault, said on Tuesday 1996 net profit rose to a preliminary 947 million tolars ($6.0 million) from 752.2 million in 1995.</p>
<p>The earnings exceeded the company's forecast of 900 million tolars and were largely boosted by higher sales, which rose to 138.6 billion tolars from 111.7 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>Production climbed to 89,229 cars from 87,513.</p>
<p>Revoz, Slovenia's top exporter last year, said it exported about 90 percent of all cars made, mainly to Germany, Italy and France.</p>
<p>Revoz is 54 percent owned by Renault and 46 percent by the Slovenian state. -- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
<p>($ = 157.3 Slovenian Tolars)</p>
